# Build-context hygiene. Critical for Dockerfile.web (context = repo root):
# keeps host node_modules from clobbering the image's freshly-installed deps,
# and keeps the context small.
#
# NOTE: codevibes-backend/ is intentionally NOT excluded — Dockerfile.web runs
# patches/apply.sh, which asserts BOTH src/hooks/useAnalysis.ts AND
# codevibes-backend/src/server.ts exist (the codemod's safety check). Only its
# node_modules/data are pruned. The backend source never reaches the final web
# image (only dist/ is copied to the caddy stage); it just needs to be present
# in the build context for the assertion to pass.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.git
.github/
dist
dist-ssr
*.log
docs/
deploy/
secrets-broker/
codevibes-backend/data/
.DS_Store
